{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "09-duplicate-definitions",
  "title": "Duplicate definitions: two scip_definition_site rows for Handler#GetJob",
  "rule_pack": "rules-static-v1",
  "provenance": {
    "kind": "synthetic",
    "source": "hand-authored adversarial static case",
    "seeded_fault": null
  },
  "context": {
    "index": "8c2d198c59483cedb430b1a48d84ed6604d1576972119a40bd3c826aea42b43e"
  },
  "review_notes": [
    "GetJob is defined at api/jobs.go:10 and again at api/jobs_legacy.go:22 (a build-tagged copy). scip_duplicate_definition derives for the pair because scip_symbol classifies GetJob as callable; the category guard (category != other) is why the scip_symbol row is a leaf of the duplicate proof.",
    "route_handler_location binds the route to api/jobs.go:10, so static_route_handler has exactly one proof and the capability is supported, with the discrepancy ambiguous-definition.",
    "scip_references_closed and static_reachability_closed are withheld for an index with duplicate definitions, so the gap claim is unresolved."
  ],
